**Not implemented / simplified from the arcade original:**

- **10-points-per-star bonus** (the arcade's star counter) is omitted — stars are purely decorative.
- Entry-path choreography uses a handful of generic curved/looping Bézier patterns per group rather than the exact per-slot arcade paths of every formation group.
- Boss dive speed does not slow down as it crosses the screen mid-dive (Galaga's signature deceleration); divers keep a constant speed.
- The captured fighter held in formation sits directly above its Boss's slot rather than displacing the formation rows.
- The title screen shows a compact score table (one line per enemy type) instead of the arcade's full two-column table with all dive/escort values, and there is no attract-mode demo play.
- Challenging-stage loop patterns are procedurally mirrored loops rather than the exact arcade wave layouts; per-wave "PERFECT" is tallied into the end-of-stage results screen rather than announced per wave.
